Inclusion Criteria
1. Subject has provided informed consent;
2. Men and women, between the ages of 18 and 55 years old, inclusive, at the time of randomization;
3. Diagnosis of SLE for at least 6 months as defined by the most recent American College of Rheumatology criteria, including a positive ANA at screening or documented positive ANA (the titer should be at least 1:80) in the past;
4. Presence of lupus related inflammatory arthritis with at least four tender and four swollen joints from a 28 joint count assessment; AND SLEDAI &#8805; 6 at screening;
5. Currently taking methotrexate, azathioprine or mycophenolate mofetil for at least 12 weeks and at a stable dose for &#8805; 4 weeks prior to randomization (other immunosuppressants including leflunomide are not allowed);
6. If the subject is on anti-malarial therapy, it should be for at least 12 weeks and at a stable dose for &#8805; 4 weeks prior to randomization;
7. Prednisone may have fluctuated but is permitted if &#8804; 10 mg/day (or comparable dose of another corticosteroid) for 4 weeks prior to screening;
8. Normal or clinically acceptable ECG (12-lead reporting ventricular rate and PR, QRS, QT, QTc) at screening based on the opinion of the investigator;
9. Body mass index from 18 to 42 kg/m2 (inclusive) at screening;
10. Immunizations up to date, with a minimum of tetanus, diphtheria, pertussis (td/Tdap), pneumococcal (polysaccharide), influenza (during flu season) and H1N1 (where and when available) vaccinations, as determined by the Principal Investigator.

Exclusion Criteria
1. Positive serology for HIV antibodies, hepatitis B surface antigen, or hepatitis C antibodies (confirmed by PCR or RIBA);
2. Evidence of signs or symptoms of a viral, bacterial, or fungal infection within 2 weeks of study randomization according to the assessment of the Investigator; history of herpes zoster in the past 3 months;
3. Known residential exposure to an individual with tuberculosis (TB) (if not treated with appropriate chemoprophylaxis) or positive Quantiferon test or positive protein purified derivative (PPD) test at screening (where a positive result is defined as induration greater than or equal to 5 mm 48-72 hours after administration) consistent with previous exposure to TB prior to or during screening. In case of prior evidence of latent infection or in case of documented BCG vaccination, eligibility will be determined in consultation with the Sponsor considering the adequacy and documentation of treatment or vaccination;
4. Donated blood or experienced a loss of blood &#8805; 500 mL within 4 weeks of randomization;
5. History of ethanol or drug abuse within the last 1 year prior to randomization;
6. Evidence of significant renal insufficiency, defined by creatinine clearance of < 50 mL/min as calculated by the Cockcroft-Gault method: (140-age) x weight [kg] x 1.23 x (0.85 if female) Serum Creatinine [micromol/l]
7. Evidence of liver disease (eg, serum ALT or AST > 1.5 x upper limit of normal);
8. Total WBC < 2500 x 106/L;
9. Neutrophil count < 2000 x 106/L;
10. Platelet count < 60,000 x 106/L;
11. Hemoglobin < 8 g/dL;
12. Presence or history of vasculitis (compromising internal organs or extremities or leading to peripheral neuropathy), presence or history of active CNS lupus (defined as seizure disorder, cerebral vascular accident, psychosis ascribed to SLE , encephalitis, meningitis, and myelitis), presence or history of active lupus nephritis requiring therapy
within the last 3 years;
13. Any disorder (including psychiatric), condition, clinically significant disease, disease activity related to SLE, or concomitant medications that would interfere with the study evaluation, completion, follow up, and/or procedures in the medical judgment of the investigator. This includes any age related co-morbidities such as congestive heart failure, angina, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, asthma, and malignancies;
14. Fibromyalgia that in the opinion of the investigator would by its nature interfere with adequate disease assessment; 
15. Uncontrolled hypertension (SBP> 150 or DBP> 95 mmHg) confirmed by repeat assessment during the screening period;
16. Poorly controlled diabetes (HbA1c > 8%);
17. Underlying condition (other than lupus) that predisposes the subject to infections (eg, history of splenectomy);
18. Any disorder or condition that prevents the subject from providing truly informed consent;
19. Received AMG 557 previously;
20. Prior administration of belimumab (or other anti-BAFF agents) in the past 3 months; rituximab (or other anti-CD20 B cell depleting agents) in the past 9 months with CD19+ B cells <5/μL; abatacept in the past 3 months; TNF inhibitors (adalimumab, certolizumab, etanercept, golimumab, infliximab) in the past 3 months; tocilizumab in the past 3 months;
21. Administration of cyclophosphamide (or any other alkylating agent), cyclosporine, tacrolimus, or sirolimus, or leflunomide in the 3 months prior to randomization;
22. Participated in an investigational drug or device trial within 30 days or 5 half-lives, whichever time period is longer, prior to randomization; 
23. Use of any other over-the-counter or prescription medications within the 14 days or 5 half-lives (whichever is longer), prior to receiving the first dose of study medication. Acetaminophen (up to 2 g per day) for analgesia and hormone replacement therapy (eg, estrogen, thyroid) will be allowed. In addition, prescription drugs for hypertension or
hypercholesterolemia, oral hypoglycemic drugs, or NSAIDs will be allowed. Other medications may be approved following review by the Principal Investigator and the Amgen Medical Monitor. Written documentation of this review and Amgen acknowledgment is required for
subject participation;
24. All herbal medicines (eg, St. John’s wort), vitamins, and supplements consumed by the subject within the 30 days prior to receiving the first dose of study medication, and continuing use if applicable, will be reviewed by the Principal Investigator and the Amgen Medical Monitor. Written documentation of this review and Amgen acknowledgment is
required for subject participation;
25. Use of nicotine or tobacco products (including but not limited to: snuff, chewing tobacco, cigars, cigarettes, pipes, or nicotine patches) in excess of 1 pack per day (20 cigarettes or the equivalent) during the study;
26. Men and women of reproductive potential, unwilling to practice a highly effective method of birth control for the duration of the study and continuing for 6 months (men) and 6 months (women) after receiving the last dose of study drug. Highly effective methods of birth control include sexual abstinence (men, women); vasectomy or a condom with spermicide (men) in combination with either barrier methods, hormonal birth control or IUD (women);
27. Women who are lactating/breastfeeding;
28. Women with a positive pregnancy test;
29. Women planning to become pregnant during the duration of the study;
30. Men with pregnant partners;
31. Subject has known sensitivity to any of the products or components to be administered during dosing.

